well since the passing of 49 year old  officer trong Tai we have learned who he  was as a police officer but today family  members are sharing are sharing with us  who he was as a brother and a son  Victoria Saha spoke with the officer's  family as they still come to terms with  his violent death with while on the job  Victoria  spending the morning with officer Ty's  family revealed what a humble person he  was and how dedicated he was to serving  this community he also protected his  family from knowing the day-to-day  dangers his job could bring and they  tell me they just celebrated his  birthday and are now planning for his  funeral  it was a very happy time we spent time  together with the help of a translator  KU Wang Tai is remembering October 6th  it would be the last time he would see  his son never thought of whatever would  happen happen we all now know him as  officer Thai but to his family he was  just Thai officer Ty was four years old  when his family immigrated to the United  States from Vietnam  really admired watching television about  police and he dreamed to be a police  since he was young a dream he turned  into a reality when he joined Metro 23  years ago the dead graduation  police officer then my family is so  proud officer Ty's sister Daisy Liu just  arrived from Hawaii despite the distance  she describes her six siblings as always  close even my best brother officer Thai  passed away last Thursday after  responding to a domestic violence call  police say Tyson Hampton fired 18 rounds  at tie and another officer one bullet  hitting officer Ty in the Torso I wish  that day if I can wake up and say I did  dreaming I wish I was there at that day  and hold his hand and say Ty we are here  for you and we all love you being killed  in the line of duty was always a fear  for Ty's family they tell me whenever  his late mom would hear of shots fired  in Las Vegas she immediately was afraid  for her son we always call him Thai okay  she said yeah I'm okay don't worry then  I we feel better but officer Tai never  wanted to back down you will not slow  down because beside him there's other  lives to take care to uh to save officer  Tai was 49 years old  officer Tai was working the graveyard  shift the morning he died it was his  shift of choice because it gave him time  to spend the day with his daughter who  his family says he adored I also asked  his father if it angered him that his  son's dream of becoming a cop ultimately  ended his life he said although they are  sad they are so proud to have a son who  gave up his life to Serve and Protect  Victoria Saha eight news now
 

